/-!
# The chart-level kernel of a graded quotient by a single-degree graded ideal

Work in Situation 01NN: a scheme `S` and a quasi-coherent graded `𝒪_S`-algebra `𝒜`. Let `ℱ` be a
quasi-coherent submodule of one homogeneous piece `𝒜_d`, and let `ψ : 𝒜 ⟶ ℬ` be a homomorphism of
graded algebras whose kernel is the graded ideal `ℱ𝒜` that `ℱ` generates, in the degreewise sense
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.IsQuotientByDegreeSubmodule`.

Over an affine open `U` of the base and away from a homogeneous section `f` of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` of
degree `e`, the homomorphism `ψ` induces a map
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map (ψ.sectionHom U) f` of degree-zero homogeneous localizations.
This file identifies its kernel with `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.chartIdeal`, the ideal generated
there by the fractions whose numerator lies in the ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)` spanned by the local
sections of `ℱ`.

That identification is the `ker_le` clause of `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ChartCuttingData`, so it
says that a quotient by `ℱ𝒜` cuts the closed subscheme out on every chart — the input that
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/DegreePresenterChart.lean` consumes.

## Main results

* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.span_degreeSectionSet_le_ker_sectionHom`: the ideal of `Γ(U, 𝒜)`
  spanned by the local sections of `ℱ` is killed by `ψ`.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.eq_zero_of_mem_generatedByDegree_of_lt`: `(ℱ𝒜)_n` vanishes below the
  generating degree.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.of_mem_span_degreeSectionSet`: **the affine-local description of
  `ℱ𝒜`.** A homogeneous local section of `ℱ𝒜` over an affine open, viewed in the graded ring of
  sections, lies in the ideal spanned by the local sections of `ℱ`.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_awayMap_sectionHom_eq_chartIdeal`: **the chart-level kernel is
  exactly `chartIdeal`.**
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.awayMk_mem_span_degreeOne`: at a degree-one `f`, a homogeneous local
  section of `ℱ𝒜` gives a fraction generated by the fractions `s / f ^ d`.
* `…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_awayMap_sectionHom_eq_span_degreeOne`: **at a degree-one `f` the
  chart-level kernel is generated by the fractions `s / f ^ d` with `s` a single local section
  of `ℱ`.**

## Implementation notes

The containment `chartIdeal ≤ ker` is the easy one: a generator is a fraction whose numerator is
killed by `ψ`, and
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.HomogeneousAwayMap.awayMk_mem_ker_awayMap_iff` applies with the
exponent `0`.

The reverse containment runs through the affine-local description of `ℱ𝒜`. A fraction in the
kernel has `f ^ j · x` in the sectionwise kernel of `ψ` for some `j`; that element is homogeneous
of degree `(k + j) • e`, hence is a single summand `ι_n w` of the graded ring of sections, and
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.sectionHom_eq_zero_iff` turns its vanishing into the vanishing of `w`.
The hypothesis `IsQuotientByDegreeSubmodule` then puts `w` in `(ℱ𝒜)_n`, and
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.mulSheafSubmodule_eq_generatedByDegree` together with
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.GabberColimit.obj_sheafSubmodule` describes `(ℱ𝒜)_n` over an affine
open as the `Γ(S, U)`-span of the products `g · b` with `g` a local section of `ℱ`. A span
induction, with `DirectSum.of_mul_of` for a generator and
`…RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra.strHom_mul_of` for the scalar step, lands `ι_n w` in the
ideal spanned by the local sections of `ℱ`. Finally
`Stacks.AlgebraicGeometry.ProjAwayBaseChange.awayMk_mulPow` rewrites the original fraction with
that numerator.

Degrees below `d` need a separate argument: there the description above would ask for a local
section of `𝒜_m` with `m < 0`, and the `negative_isZero` field of a
`…RelativeProjBridge.SheafGradedAlgebra` makes that piece a zero object, so `(ℱ𝒜)_n` vanishes.
That vanishing field of the situation datum is used here and nowhere else in this file.

The two spellings `((d + m : ℕ) : ℤ)` and `(d : ℤ) + (m : ℤ)` of a degree are definitionally
equal and are used interchangeably, as in
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjBridge/SectionRing.lean`.

**The degree-one refinement** is not a span manipulation applied to `chartIdeal`, which would
have to split a numerator lying in the ideal spanned by the local sections of `ℱ` into
homogeneous components. It is the same induction run one level up: the generators of the
affine-local description of `ℱ𝒜` are *already* a product of a degree-`d` factor from `ℱ` with a
factor of complementary degree, and the span is over `Γ(S, U)` only, so each step of the
induction produces a multiple of a single fraction `s / f ^ d` rather than a new generator. The
fraction arithmetic that the step needs is `…awayMk_mul_eq` and `…awayMk_add_eq`, collected
below with the target exponent and the numerator of the result as free arguments so that no
rewrite under `HomogeneousLocalization.Away.mk` is ever needed, together with the congruence
`ProjChartBaseChange.awayMk_congr` and the zero case `ProjBaseChange.awayMk_zero`, which are
taken as they stand.

## Not done here

No Stacks tag is claimed: the statements below are about the kernel of Mathlib's
`HomogeneousLocalization.Away.map`, and the Stacks tags that consume them (0801, 0802) are proved
elsewhere. Nothing here constructs the quotient algebra `𝒜/ℱ𝒜`, nor compares the chart kernel
with the kernel of a graded quotient map; that comparison is
`…RelativeProjGradedIdeal.ker_awayMap_sectionHom_eq` of
`StacksFrontier/AlgebraicGeometry/RelativeProjGradedIdeal/DegreePresenterChart.lean`.
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

